// The gate the build runs, as opposed to the one an editor runs.
//
// `vite build` does not typecheck, so without this a bundle referencing a
// variable that does not exist compiles cleanly and then throws
// `ReferenceError` on first render — which unmounts React and leaves a blank
// page with nothing in the console. That shipped once; this is what stops it.
//
// It keeps `strict` and every correctness check, and drops only
// `noUnusedLocals`: an unused local is untidy, never broken, and half-built
// scaffolding routinely has some. Blocking a release on it would just teach
// people to bypass the gate.
{
  "extends": "./tsconfig.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "noUnusedLocals": false
  }
}
